    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The deputy general director of the online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for distributing the film “Yves Saint Laurent” (Jalil Lespert, 2014). The court described 23 scenes in this film “touching on the topic of non-traditional sexual relations and (or) preferences”. Among these scenes are dialogs, “nonverbal prolonged glances”, kissing, hugging, and sexual interaction between “persons of the same biological sex”. The judicial expertise stated that the film presented “non-traditional sexual relationships as a basic condition for the development of a fashion designer's talent and the success of a fashion house, thereby aestheticizing non-traditional sexual relationships.” The time codes of the scenese mentioned by the court are: 00:09:27-00:10:35, 00:20:22-00:21:12, 00:22:14-00:23:25, 00:23:07-00:23:13, 00:14:25-00:14:30, 00:23:38-00:23:56, 00:26:15-00:26:28, 00:26:31-00:26:43, 00:29:52-00:30:52, 00:31:08-00:32:02, 00:42:29-00:42:41, 00:43:53-00:44:18, 00:49:49-00:50:29, 00:57:53-00:58:13, 00:58:18-00:58:20, 00:59:59-01:00:24, 01:03:34-01:04:27, 01:10:06-01:10:55, 01:14:21-01:15:05, 01:15:25-01:16:21, 01:17:10-01:18:19, 01:18:48- 01:19:09, 01:20:09-01:21:19.</dataout:hasSnippet>
