    <dataout:hasPenalty>
      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_c7c61033">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a picture of “two women on the backdrop of a flag, which is the symbol of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'” in 2019. The court described the content of the picture: “two women standing opposite each other in a public place against the backdrop of a flag consisting of six stripes, the colors of which, from top to bottom, are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple; the women' faces are turned toward each other, their mouths open and their tongues sticking out.” The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), [...] it is expressed visually (the viewer is shown that this is beautiful, aesthetically pleasing, and therefore good and acceptable); [...] sexual relations not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for public display, on par with heterosexual ones.” The exact picture is unknown. The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown.</dataout:hasSnippet>
