    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A VKontakte user was fined after police identified a publicly accessible photograph on his page and classified it as “LGBT propaganda.” The ruling contains no description of the image itself: neither subject matter, text, symbols, nor persons depicted are recorded in the judgment. The finding of liability rests entirely on the police classification of the linked photograph as material related to “non-traditional sexual relations”. The exact image is unavailable.</dataout:hasSnippet>
