    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The streaming service “Kinopoisk” was fined for four films “Dr. T &amp; the Women” (2000, Robert Altman), “Little Italy” (2018, Donald Petrie), “Alexander” (2004, Oliver Stone), and “Love Is Love Is Love” (2020, Eleanor Coppola). According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations or preferences” to minors. The exact scenes are unclear.</dataout:hasSnippet>
