    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The company “M3”, which owns the streaming service “More.tv”, was fined for two films: “Three Many Weddings” (Javier Ruiz Caldera, 2013) and “Blow Dry” (Paddy Breathnach, 2001), both labelled “16+”. According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors. The experts from Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found eight scenes with such demonstration in the first title (the exact time codes are 00:56:57-00:58:20, 00:58:21-00:58:52, 01:00:12-01:01:33, 01:01:34-01:02:10, 01:02:11-01:03:29, 01:04:14-01:04:22, 01:06:19-01:06:34, 01:10:32-01:11:00). In the second title, the experts identified one scene (01:21:47-01:21:57), in which “two characters of the same sex (female) kissing in a sexual context.” The deputy general director of the company was also fined for the same content (see case 5-940/23).</dataout:hasSnippet>
