        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The TV channel “Zhara TV” was fined for broadcasting the music video “Girls” (2018) by Rita Ora featuring Cardi B, Bebe Rexha, and Charli XCX to minors under a 16+ age rating. The judgment treated the clip as a multimodal audiovisual text and closely described its visual composition, noting first a sequence in which women dressed in light-coloured garments sing together, communicate, and exchange gestures of affection, while “the atmosphere of what is happening is hedonistic” and the overall imagery is “perceived as an ancient Greek Sapphic salon.” A second sequence was analysed separately: one female figure observes another through holographic imagery, the two move closer, and their interaction is presented at “an intimate interpersonal distance” involving “touching, as well as a kiss on the lips.” These quoted visual observations formed the core of the court’s reasoning that the clip demonstrated “non-traditional sexual relations” and therefore could not lawfully remain accessible to minors under a 16+ classification. Earlier, the editor-in-chief of this TV channel was fined for the same music video (see case 5-955/23).</dataout:hasSnippet>
