    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The editor-in-chief of the “KinoLiving” TV channel was fined after Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that the TV channel aired the series “Episodes” (David Crane and Jeffrey Klarik, 2011), which “contained information demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences expressed by a visual component: an image of sensual interaction between two persons of the same biological sex (female), prolonged kisses and caresses of two women.”</dataout:hasSnippet>
