        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for three TV-series, labelled “16+”, which “contained a demonstration of non-traditional sexual relations and preferences”. As the St. Petersburg courts press office stated, the TV series “Annika” (Nick Walker, 2021) contained dialogs “referencing to non-traditional sexual relations” in episodes 2, 5, and 6. In the episode 4, there was “even a demonstration in the form of a kiss”. In the series “The One and Only” (Moon Jung-min, 2021), there were “bad scenes where one woman gently strokes the hand of another”. And the series “My Dead Ex” (Drew Hancock, 2018) “was let down by [..] a character's coming out”.</dataout:hasSnippet>
