    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for the film “Yves Saint Laurent” (Jalil Lespert, 2014). According to the Head of the St. Petersburg courts press office, there were multiple scenes identified in the film containing “propaganda of LGBT”, including these scenes: “two people of the same sex passionately kissing; '–What a cutie he is! –Forget it! He's into guys; -Where are the bedrooms?, -There's only one, -So you're together?, -Yes”; “two people of the same biological sex kissing, accompanied by a voice-over commentary 'I believed in the cult of fidelity, but with you everything happened incredibly quickly'.” The deputy general director of this streaming service was also fined for the same film (case 5-837/2024-162).</dataout:hasSnippet>
