        <schema:name xml:lang="en">Managing director of the streaming service “Kinopoisk”</schema:name>
        <schema:name xml:lang="ru">Генеральный директор, руководитель отдела ООО “Кинопоиск”</schema:name>
      </dataout:Defendant>
    </dataout:hasDefendant>
    <dataout:hasPenalty>
      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_3f538d08">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
        <dataout:penaltyValue>
          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b86">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">250000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The managing director of the streaming service “Kinopoisk” was fined for the film “Triggered” (Christopher Wesley Moore, 2019). The court stated that this film contains information “promoting non-traditional sexual relations”, as it features “footage of interaction between two characters of the same biological sex (male); Viewing these scenes creates an intimate and personal mood for subsequent intersexual relations; The fragments contain depictions of romantic relationships, including images of sexual intercourse, accompanied by music and dialogue, with humorous references to the characters' non-traditional sexual preferences”. The court also mentioned that the two main characters were portrayed as “positive with a range of positive qualities, such as kindness, understanding, and responsiveness. Relationships between characters of the same biological sex are presented in a romantic vein.”</dataout:hasSnippet>
