        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A VKontakte user was fined for publishing “a semi-nude photograph of two men embracing.” In this image, the judicial experts identified “linguistic and psychological signs of propaganda for non-traditional sexual relations [...] expressed in the display of love and sexual scenes between two men in an aesthetically appealing manner with the aim of arousing interest in such contacts.” The exact images are unclear; the profile has been deleted. This individual was fined at least three times by the same judge on the same day for posting on VKontakte and was also detained for 15 days for posting images depicting rainbow flags, which the court deemed as “public demonstration of extremist symbols” (article 20.3).</dataout:hasSnippet>
