      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A VKontakte user was fined for “an image with the English-language text 'Some people are gay, get over it'”, which is a slogan of the Stonewall UK campaign from 2007. The image was published on VK in 2013. According to the court, this image “disseminated information aimed at developing non-traditional sexual attitudes in minors”. The exact image is unknown. The same individual was fined twice on the same day by the same judge for publishing images on VK (see also 05-0211/2025).</dataout:hasSnippet>
