    <dataout:hasPenalty>
      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_570518d4">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
        <dataout:penaltyValue>
          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b104">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">200000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The deputy general director for content on the streaming service “Ivi” was fined for the films “Little Italy” (Donald Petrie, 2018), “Dr. T &amp; the Women” (Robert Altman, 2000), “Love Is Love Is Love” (Eleanor Coppola, 2021), and “Beginners” (Mike Mills, 2011) with the age restriction label “16+”. The court mentioned that these films contained “scenes describing homosexual relationships between men and [...] women, as well as references to homosexual relationships” demonstrating “non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors. It is not specified which scenes exactly constituted the violation. The company that owns the streaming service was also fined for the same films (case 05-0902/2023).</dataout:hasSnippet>
