      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The “Yandex” CEO Artem Savinovsky was fined because the company's streaming service “Kinopoisk” showed such films as “Dr. T &amp; the Women” (Robert Altman, 2000), “Little Italy” (Donald Petrie, 2018), “Alexander” (Oliver Stone, 2004), and “Love Is Love Is Love” (Eleanor Coppola, 2021) with the age restriction label “16+”. According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” and should have been marked “18+”. The court did not specify the exact scenes in these movies that constituted the violation. </dataout:hasSnippet>
