      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The general director and editor-in-chief of the TV channel “EuroKino” was fined for airing the film “French Women” (Audrey Dana, 2014), labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found the film to contain “information demonstrating non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences, which is expressed by a verbal component (dialogues between two women), a visual component: an image of sensual interaction between two women, where scenes are shown containing tactile communication after sexual interaction, prolonged kisses.” The company, which owns the TV channel, was also fined for the same film (see case 05-0835/2023).</dataout:hasSnippet>
