    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">An individual was fined for “statements [...] aimed at developing non-traditional sexual attitudes, the attractiveness of non-traditional sexual relationships and preferences, sex change, a distorted idea of the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relationships and preferences, arousing interest in such relationships and preferences, and sex change.” The court redacted the exact content that constituted the violation. In the evidence list, there was a screenshot of the correspondence in a messenger app mentioned. However, the exact messages are unknown. According to the mass media, this case was against a trans woman, who was fined after her classmates complained about the fact that she supported Ukraine and LGBTQ+ rights.</dataout:hasSnippet>
