          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b135">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">200000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">An official at the streaming service “Kinopoisk” was fined for distributing two films, “Breaking Up in Rome” (Edoardo Leo, 2021) and “Clouds of Sils Maria” (Olivier Assayas, 2014), labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that these films contained “information and scenes demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, where men kiss on the lips, as well as scenes with dialogue between characters that touch on the topic of non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, in particular homosexual relations.”</dataout:hasSnippet>
