    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">“RED Media” was fined for broadcasting the music video “Город” (“The City”) by the band “Tantsy Minus” (2013) to minors on its TV channel “La Minor TV”. According to the court, it “contained material demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations”. Rejecting the defence argument that the video merely depicted friendship and affection for Russian cities, the court focused on a scene where one female character, in its words, “sensually interacts with another female person”, treating that moment as the central evidentiary basis for liability. The judgment also moved beyond ordinary legal description by offering an extended semiotic reading of the clip, calling it a “polycode (creolised) text”, discussing “clip culture”, and interpreting the montage as a symbolic narrative of memory, emotion, and desire before concluding that same-sex intimacy embedded in that audiovisual sequence could not lawfully remain classified as suitable for children aged twelve and above.</dataout:hasSnippet>
