    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The film distribution company “Russian Report” was fined for airing the TV series “Made in Italy” (Camilla Nesbitt, 2019) on the “KinoLiving” TV channel with the label “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that the fifth episode of the TV series “contained information (visual) consistent with the signs of demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, [...] conveyed through verbal and visual components: the address ‘honey’ [...] and displyas of a kiss and hug”, which, according to the court, is prohibited to distribute among minors.</dataout:hasSnippet>
