            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1000000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The company that owns the streaming service “Ivi” was fined for the films “Little Italy” (Donald Petrie, 2018), “Dr. T &amp; the Women” (Robert Altman, 2000), “Love Is Love Is Love” (Eleanor Coppola, 2021), and “Beginners” (Mike Mills, 2011), all labelled “16+”. The court found that these films “contained information demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, which is prohibited for distribution among children.” It is not specified which scenes exactly constituted the violation.</dataout:hasSnippet>
