    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The court fined the deputy general director for content on the streaming service “Ivi” for the film “Perfect Strangers” (Paolo Genovese, 2016). According to Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, the film “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors, because it was labelled “16+”. It is not specified which scenes exactly constituted the violation. The company which owns the streaming service was also fined for the same film (case 05-0771/2023).</dataout:hasSnippet>
