    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The deputy general director of the online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for distributing the film “Triggered” (2019, Christopher Moore). The judicial expertise established that “the genre, plot, and expressive means used [in the film] aimed at fostering a positive attitude toward non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences; The depicted same-sex relationships and the storyline are structured in such a way as to create a socio-psychological attitude not only toward the attractiveness of non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences, but also to foster a distorted perception of the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relationships”. The streaming platform was also fined for the same film (see case 5-1661/2025).</dataout:hasSnippet>
