      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_1dafe1b3">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
        <dataout:penaltyValue>
          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b41">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">500000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The TV channel “AIVA” was fined for airing the music video “Tak Krasivo” (“So Beautiful”) by Sergey Lazarev (2017). The court did not publish the text of the decision. According to the mass media, the protocol stated that the video “demonstrated interacting hands (caressing each other), the position of which as well as their individual characteristics (hair, shape of the nail plate, manicure, jewelry) show that they belong to two people of the same-sex, which can be potentially perceived as a tactile, sensual interaction of persons conveying their homosexual preferences”, and that the video communicates “that people in non-traditional sexual relationships are not only no different from representatives of heterosexual relationships, but their preferences, if not socially approved, are at least acceptable in society and equivalent to the union of a man and a woman.” The editor-in-chief of this TV channel was also fined 200,000 RUB for the same video, as the media reported. However, we could not obtain the corresponding court decision.</dataout:hasSnippet>
