    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The deputy general director of the online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for distributing three TV series, labelled “16+”, which “contained a demonstration of non-traditional sexual relations and preferences”. In the TV series “Annika” (Nick Walker, 2021), court identified 4 scenes, in which characters “mention non-traditional sexual orientation”, and one of the scenes depicted two women kissing: 39:31-39:33 (episode 2); 38:26-38:45 (episode 4); 23:32-23:43 (episode 5); 00:28-00:30 (episode 6). In the series “The One and Only” (Moon Jung-min, 2021), the court mentioned 4 scenes, in one of them, a woman gently strokes the hand of another: 00:22:30-00:27:03, 00:45:45-00:46:00 (episode 9); 00:36:21-00:36:59 (episode 10); 00:17:05-00:18:38 (episode 11). In the series “My Dead Ex” (Drew Hancock, 2018), there were also four scenes mentioned, in which characters talk about “non-traditional sexual preferences”, women kissing, and a character comes out as a lesbian: 00:40-00:58 (episode 1); 14:40-15:11 (episode 4); 26:02-26:33 (episode 6); 15:56-17:20 (episode 8). The streaming platform was also fined for the same series (see case 5-253/2024).</dataout:hasSnippet>
