    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A school principal was fined for a banner dedicated to International Tolerance Day placed in the school hallway. The photo of this banner was published on Telegram, which led to an investigation. One of the pieces of evidence the court admitted was a “comprehensive psycho-cultural examination”, which found the banner made by students to contain “symbols of LGBD-community” and “signs of promotion of non-traditional sexual relations among minors.”</dataout:hasSnippet>
