    <dataout:hasDefendant rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#1197746708917"/>
    <dataout:hasPenalty>
      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_412bf1d3">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
        <dataout:penaltyValue>
          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b88">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">4000000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The streaming service “PREMIER” was fined for the films “Perfect Strangers” (Paolo Genovese, 2016) and “Blow Dry” (2001, Paddy Breathnach). According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors, because they were labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, identified eight scenes in the first film (00:58:46–00:59:09, 01:01:05–01:01:35, 01:01:36–01:03:50, 01:04:32–01:04:55, 01:05:56–01:06:35, 01:17:24–01:17:29, 01:17:40–01:20:40, 01:22:10–01:22:21) “demonstrating (or describing) homosexual relations between men, as well as references to homosexual relationships.” In the film “Blow Dry”, Roskomnadzor found the scene (01:21:45-01:22:01) with “two characters of the same sex (female) kissing in a sexual context.”</dataout:hasSnippet>
