    <dataout:concernsLegalArticle rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_law#article_6_21_part_3"/>
    <dataout:hasDefendant rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#individual_0077"/>
    <dataout:hasPenalty>
      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_5faf36f4">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a picture of “two women kissing in front of a flag with the symbols of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'” in 2019. The court described the picture as “in the foreground, two womem are shown facing each other in close proximity; in the background, a canvas is partially displayed, on which stripes are visible, the colors of which go from top to bottom - red, orange, yellow, green.” The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), [...] it is expressed visually (the viewer is shown that this is beautiful, aesthetically pleasing, and therefore good and acceptable); [...] sexual relations not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for public display, on par with heterosexual ones.” The exact picture is unknown. The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown. </dataout:hasSnippet>
