      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_e07a8a94">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
        <dataout:penaltyValue>
          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b235">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">450000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The company “Elton John Krasnoyarsk”, which owns the queer club “Elton”, was fined for “propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences and sex change during [...] ‘drag queen shows’.” The police came to the club after a complaint was filed against it. During their visit, the police noticed that the drag show “featured male participants dressed as females [...] interacting with bar clients.” They also determined that “some same-sex visitors engaged in non-traditional sexual behaviour (hugging and kissing each other on the lips) [...] directed at an unspecified number of visitors present within the premises.” Among the pieces of evidence the court reviewed were security camera recordings inside the club, which were described as “male bar visitors hugging and kissing each other in front of the stage”, “a male figure dressed in women's clothing, a dress, a wig, and bright makeup, stands near the stage in front of the sofas, interacting with male visitors”, and “near the bar counter, two women are hugging and kissing each other on the lips.”</dataout:hasSnippet>
