    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The company “Gramota”, which owns the bookshop chain “Chitai gorod”, was fined for selling the graphic novel “Immortal” (“Bes/smertniy” by Koriandr, Eksmo, 2023). The court found that the book “had signs of promoting non-traditional sexual relations.” According to the judicial expertise carried out by the Crimean Engineering and Pedagogical University, the book “depicts psychological and physical (sexual) violence, with men serving as both subjects and objects (Koschei – Ivan; Prince – Koschei; Ivan – Sergei). Both the villain (Koschei) and the hero (Ivan) identify non-traditionally in terms of gender.” Among other pieces of evidence in this case was a police report submitted by the bookshop customer.</dataout:hasSnippet>
