      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_37163b21">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
        <dataout:penaltyValue>
          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b71">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">50000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A creator of a community page on VKontakte was fined for “publications with text and photographs, accessible to an unlimited number of people (at the time of monitoring, the group had 2,945 members), aimed at the formation of non-traditional sexual relations and preferences, a distorted idea of the societal value of traditional and non-traditional sexual relations.” The exact publications are unknown. The defence stated that the website, on which the individual published the images, was labelled “18+”, but the court dismissed it. Initially, a magistrate fined the defendant 100,000 RUB, but the higher instance judge reduced the fine.</dataout:hasSnippet>
