    <prov:wasGeneratedBy rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#MonitoringDec2025"/>
    <dataout:concernsLegalArticle rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_law#article_6_21_2_part_2"/>
    <dataout:hasDefendant rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#official_0029"/>
    <dataout:hasPenalty rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_08e64d17"/>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The deputy director general of the streaming service “PREMIER” was fined for the films “Perfect Strangers” (Paolo Genovese, 2016) and “Blow Dry” (2001, Paddy Breathnach). According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors, because they were labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, identified eight scenes in the first film (00:58:46–00:59:09, 01:01:05–01:01:35, 01:01:36–01:03:50, 01:04:32–01:04:55, 01:05:56–01:06:35, 01:17:24–01:17:29, 01:17:40–01:20:40, 01:22:10–01:22:21) “demonstrating (or describing) homosexual relations between men, as well as references to homosexual relationships.” In the film “Blow Dry”, Roskomnadzor found the scene (01:21:45-01:22:01) with “two characters of the same sex (female) kissing in a sexual context.” Earlier, the company, which owns the streaming service, was fined for the same content (see case 05-1040/2023).</dataout:hasSnippet>
