        <dataout:uniqueCourtDocumentID>77MS0222-01-2024-002694-62</dataout:uniqueCourtDocumentID>
      </dataout:Source>
    </prov:wasDerivedFrom>
    <prov:wasGeneratedBy rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#MonitoringDec2025"/>
    <dataout:concernsLegalArticle rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_law#article_6_21_part_3"/>
    <dataout:hasDefendant rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#individual_0077"/>
    <dataout:hasPenalty rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_abd0b352"/>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a picture of “two women, one of whom is kissing the other, and symbols similar to those of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'” in 2019. The court described the content of the picture: “in the lower left corner are two women, one of whom is kneeling, holding a rose in her left hand and placing a ring on the other woman's finger; in the upper right corner, one women is kissing the other women on the cheek; in the left corner, [...] there is a pattern of stripes [...] red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple; in the lower right corner, [...] there is the text 'yes, I am from Russia'.” The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), [...] it is expressed visually (the viewer is shown that it is beautiful, youthful, fashionable, modern, daring, informal, it is a challenge and therefore good and acceptable); [...] sexual relations not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for public display on an equal basis with heterosexual relations”. The exact picture is unknown. The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown.</dataout:hasSnippet>
