    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The TV channel “KINO TV” was fined for “distributing among minors” the film “V for Vendetta” (James McTeigue, 2006), labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, which carried out judicial expertise, found four scenes in the film “demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations.” Such scenes “expressed verbal (description) and visual components (images of kisses, hugs between persons of the same biological sex (female).” Earlier, the editor-in-chief of this TV channel was fined for the same film (see case 12-1609/2023).</dataout:hasSnippet>
