        <schema:legalName xml:lang="ru">ООО “Точка ТВ”</schema:legalName>
      </dataout:Defendant>
    </dataout:hasDefendant>
    <dataout:hasPenalty>
      <dataout:Penalty rdf:about="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_60f16dde">
        <dataout:penaltyCategory rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/ontology#fine"/>
        <dataout:penaltyValue>
          <schema:MonetaryAmount rdf:nodeID="nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b111">
            <schema:currency>RUB</schema:currency>
            <schema:value rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">1000000</schema:value>
          </schema:MonetaryAmount>
        </dataout:penaltyValue>
      </dataout:Penalty>
    </dataout:hasPenalty>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The TV channel “TOCHKA TV” was fined for airing the music video “Stranger” (2012) by Nikolai Baskov, labelled “16+”. The court stated that this video “contained information demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” and should have had the label “18+”. The experts from Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, identified six scenes in the music video, which show a relationship story between two men placed in the “atmosphere of hedonism and debauchery, which is realised primarily through repeated scenes of non-verbal sensual interaction between two persons of the same biological sex (female) in a sexual context.” The editor-in-chief of this TV channel was also fined for the same content (see case 5-998/23).</dataout:hasSnippet>
