    <dataout:hasPenalty rdf:resource="https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_419b8f28"/>
    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">The journalist Elena Klimova created the online support project “Children-404. LGBT-teenagers”, which included groups on social media, in which queer teens shared their experiences and sought support. The project regularly published their letters. The court determined that the project’s content constituted unlawful promotion of same-sex relationships among minors. In 2025, the European Court of Human Rights ruled that the decision of the Russian court violates the Articles 8 and 10 of the ECHR.</dataout:hasSnippet>
