    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A Tajikistan citizen was detained for 10 days and ordered to leave the country for posts on Telegram, which, according to the court, were “aimed at developing non-traditional sexual attitudes.” The court stated that in these posts the defendant “offered intimate services, posing as a 'transsexual', a person who partially changed sex.” The exact content that constituted the violation is unknown.</dataout:hasSnippet>
