    <dataout:hasSnippet xml:lang="en">A Moscow resident was fined for a VKontakte video titled “Red and anarcho skinheads fight straights until complete victory.” The court classified the upload as “LGBT propaganda” without explaining the video’s visual content, context, or date of origin. The video was uploaded over 10 years before the ruling, and it shows skinheads and anarchist gatherings. As in the parallel rulings (case 05-0719/2025), liability was based primarily on the title and public accessibility of the material rather than on any detailed analysis of what the recording actually depicted. The same individual was fined at least twice for different online content.</dataout:hasSnippet>
